&lt;p&gt;Unspecified&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A fish-curing factory (&lt;em&gt;salsamenta&lt;/em&gt;) located to the SE of the Nymfarum domus was renovated between the 2nd and the 3rd centuries. Among the changes made was the design of a small house organized around a small peristyle garden (4 x 4 m.) (XXII) and bound by a low wall that curved to make a semi-circular basin (Plan view, Fig.1; ).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;During the second half of the 4th century, with the abandonment of the industrial unit, the residential area was enlarged and a second semi-circular basin was added in the garden.&lt;/p&gt;
